 "after": "Notice how the verb sits at the end of every sentence: پیشی ماهی را دوست دارد – 'Pishi fish (object) likes'. The little word را after ماهی marks the fish as the thing that is liked; you will study it properly at A2. Persian pet names are often playful: پیشی (Pishi) is simply what Iranians call to a cat, like 'kitty'. The same word شیر means both 'milk' and 'lion' – only the context tells you which. Goldfish are everywhere in Iran: a bowl of red fish, like Mina's, sits on every Nowruz table.",
 "titleV": "گُربه و ماهی",
 "titleA": "5a280f9bdefa"
}
